const realms=[
{name:'The Ember Workshop',cert:'A+',role:'The Artificer',icon:'✦',desc:'Restore forgotten machines. Master hardware, operating systems, and the art of troubleshooting.',spell:'Mending Light',effect:'Recover 26 health once per battle.',chapters:[
['A spark in the ruins','Components & power','The Clockwork Imp','A computer brings specialized components together. RAM is volatile working memory: its contents disappear when power is lost. An SSD keeps files without power. The power supply converts incoming AC power to the DC power used by internal components. Before servicing internal hardware, shut down, unplug power, and use appropriate ESD protection.',[
['Which component loses its contents when power is removed?',['RAM','SSD','Firmware flash','Hard drive'],0,'RAM is volatile working memory; persistent storage retains data without power.'],['What converts AC power into DC for internal components?',['CPU','Power supply','Network adapter','Heat sink'],1,'The power supply converts and distributes power.'],['Before replacing internal hardware, what should you do first?',['Open every app','Disconnect power safely','Remove the CPU immediately','Format the drive'],1,'Shut down and disconnect power before internal service; also follow ESD precautions.']]],
['The frozen archive','Operating systems & recovery','The Kernel Wraith','An operating system manages hardware, memory, files, and applications. Drivers let the OS communicate with devices. When a problem begins after a driver update, rolling back that driver may restore operation. Back up important data before changes that could destroy it. Use the least disruptive reasonable troubleshooting step first.',[
['What enables an operating system to communicate with a device?',['A driver','A ZIP archive','An HDMI cable alone','A browser cookie'],0,'A driver provides the device-specific interface to the operating system.'],['A device fails immediately after a driver update. What is a reasonable recovery step?',['Replace every component','Roll back the driver','Delete all user files','Disable every service'],1,'A rollback targets the recent change without broad destructive action.'],['Before reinstalling an OS in a way that erases data, you should…',['Back up important files','Turn off the monitor','Clear browser history only','Remove the keyboard'],0,'A verified backup protects data before a destructive reinstall.']]],
['Heart of the forge','Troubleshooting & support','The Iron Colossus','Troubleshooting starts by identifying the problem and gathering information. Establish a likely cause, then test your theory. Plan and implement a solution, verify full functionality, and document what happened. Excess heat can cause instability; inspect cooling and airflow. A known-good cable can help isolate a connection problem.',[
['What is the first troubleshooting step?',['Replace the motherboard','Identify the problem','Reinstall everything','Document a fix you have not tested'],1,'Gather symptoms, recent changes, and relevant details before choosing a fix.'],['A computer shuts down under heavy load and feels very hot. What should you inspect?',['Desktop wallpaper','Cooling and airflow','Font settings','Browser bookmarks'],1,'Poor cooling can cause overheating and protective shutdowns.'],['After implementing a fix, what should you do?',['Assume it worked','Verify functionality and document','Delete the backup','Skip user feedback'],1,'Verify the solution and record the outcome.']]]]},
{name:'The Sapphire Crossing',cert:'Network+',role:'The Wayfinder',icon:'⌘',desc:'Reconnect the scattered kingdoms. Learn addressing, routing, and the paths between worlds.',spell:'Restoration Flask',effect:'Drink your equipped Network+ potion once per battle. Upgrades restore 25, 40, then 60 HP without an enemy counterattack.',chapters:[
['Names across the mist','Network services','The DNS Specter','DNS resolves names to records such as IP addresses. DHCP can automatically assign IP configuration to clients. A default gateway forwards traffic toward destinations outside the local subnet. If a host can reach a server by IP but not by name, investigate name resolution.',[
['Which service resolves hostnames to IP addresses?',['DHCP','DNS','NTP','SSH'],1,'DNS supplies name resolution.'],['Which service can automatically assign client IP configuration?',['DNS','HTTPS','DHCP','SMTP'],2,'DHCP leases addresses and can supply options such as a gateway and DNS servers.'],['A server works by IP but not by hostname. What should you investigate?',['DNS resolution','Monitor brightness','Keyboard layout','CPU cooling'],0,'Working IP connectivity with failing names points toward name resolution.']]],
['The divided bridge','Switching & routing','The Loop Hydra','A switch forwards Ethernet frames using MAC addresses. A router forwards IP packets between networks. VLANs create separate logical broadcast domains; communication between them generally needs routing. A /24 IPv4 network has a 255.255.255.0 subnet mask and typically 254 usable host addresses in a conventional subnet.',[
['What does an Ethernet switch primarily use to forward frames?',['MAC addresses','Domain names','File extensions','Passwords'],0,'Switches learn MAC addresses and associate them with ports.'],['Which device forwards packets between IP networks?',['Passive splitter','Router','Keyboard','Patch panel alone'],1,'Routers select paths between networks using IP routing information.'],['What subnet mask corresponds to /24?',['255.0.0.0','255.255.0.0','255.255.255.0','255.255.255.252'],2,'A /24 prefix has 24 network bits set to one.']]],
['Storm over the gateway','Ports & diagnostics','The Tempest Leviathan','HTTPS commonly uses TCP port 443 and provides encrypted web communication. SSH commonly uses TCP port 22 for secure remote command-line access. Ping uses ICMP echo to test reachability, though firewalls can block it. Traceroute discovers intermediate hops using TTL or hop-limit behavior; silence alone does not prove a destination is down.',[
['Which port is commonly used for HTTPS?',['21','25','443','110'],2,'HTTPS commonly uses TCP 443.'],['What is SSH commonly used for?',['Secure remote command-line access','Allocating DHCP leases','Analog audio','Public DNS registration'],0,'SSH provides an encrypted remote administration channel, usually on TCP 22.'],['A host does not answer ping. What can you conclude?',['It is definitely broken','Its firewall may block ICMP','Its SSD is full','DNS must be offline'],1,'A missing echo reply is not proof of an offline host; ICMP may be filtered.']]]]},
{name:'The Obsidian Citadel',cert:'Security+',role:'The Sentinel',icon:'♜',desc:'Break the shadow pact. Wield identity, defense, and incident response against the darkness.',spell:'Cipher Strike',effect:'Deal 26 damage once per battle.',chapters:[
['The stolen sigil','Identity & access','The Mimic Knight','Least privilege gives users only the access needed for their work. MFA uses different factor categories, such as something you know and something you have. Two passwords are still the same factor type. Phishing impersonates a trusted source to trick people into revealing information or taking an unsafe action. Verify unexpected requests through a trusted independent channel.',[
['What does least privilege mean?',['Everyone is an administrator','Only necessary access is granted','Passwords are shared','Access never expires'],1,'Limit permissions to what a person or service needs.'],['Which is an example of different authentication factor types?',['Two passwords','Password and hardware security key','PIN and password','Two security questions'],1,'A password is knowledge; a hardware key is possession.'],['An urgent message asks for credentials. What is a good response?',['Send the password','Verify through a trusted independent channel','Forward it to everyone','Disable MFA'],1,'Verify independently and follow your reporting process.']]],
['Secrets beneath stone','Cryptography & defense','The Cipher Basilisk','Encryption protects confidentiality by transforming data using a key. Hashing creates a digest used for purposes such as detecting changes; it is not reversible encryption. A firewall permits or denies traffic according to rules. Defense in depth layers controls so that a single failed defense does not leave everything exposed.',[
['Which property does encryption primarily protect?',['Confidentiality','Monitor resolution','CPU speed','File naming'],0,'Encryption keeps data unreadable without the appropriate key.'],['What is a cryptographic hash commonly used for?',['Detecting data changes','Reversibly hiding a password','Replacing all backups','Increasing bandwidth'],0,'Comparing digests can help check integrity.'],['What is defense in depth?',['One very long password only','Multiple complementary security layers','Removing all logs','Using one firewall for every problem'],1,'Layered controls reduce reliance on any single defense.']]],
['The final breach','Incident response & resilience','The Shadow Sovereign','When responding to an incident, follow the established response plan. Containment limits spread and damage; eradication removes the cause, and recovery restores safe operation. Preserve evidence and record actions. Backups must be tested to establish that restoration works. Ransomware can encrypt files and may also steal data, so recovery and investigation both matter.',[
['What is the purpose of incident containment?',['Limit spread and damage','Erase all evidence','Publish credentials','Skip investigation'],0,'Containment limits impact while the response proceeds.'],['How do you establish that a backup is usable?',['Trust its filename','Perform a tested restoration','Only check its icon','Never open it'],1,'Restoration testing verifies that data can actually be recovered.'],['During incident handling, you should…',['Document actions and preserve evidence','Delete logs immediately','Ignore the response plan','Share secrets publicly'],0,'Records and preserved evidence support investigation and recovery.']]]]}];
// Keep original questions first so legacy pending-question indices remain valid.
for(let c=0;c<3;c++){
 const extra=STUDY_QUESTIONS.filter(q=>!Array.isArray(q.answer)&&(c===0?q.core===1&&q.domain<4:c===1?q.core===2&&q.domain===1:q.core===1&&q.domain===5||q.core===2&&q.domain>1));
 extra.sort((a,b)=>(a.id.startsWith('detail:')?2:a.id.endsWith('-applied-case-v2')?1:0)-(b.id.startsWith('detail:')?2:b.id.endsWith('-applied-case-v2')?1:0));
 realms[0].chapters[c][4].push(...extra.map(q=>[q.prompt,q.options,q.answer,q.explanation]));
}
realms.push(...CLOUD_REALMS);
function questCount(){return realms.reduce((sum,r)=>sum+r.chapters.length,0);}
function validQuest(r,c){return Number.isInteger(r)&&Number.isInteger(c)&&!!realms[r]?.chapters[c];}
const KEY='certquest.v1';const fresh=()=>({version:1,hero:0,heroChosen:false,gearRevision:3,inventory:[],equipment:{weapon:null,armor:null,potion:null,charm:null,shield:null},xp:0,gold:0,done:[],read:[],battle:null,correct:0,answered:0});let state=fresh(),storageOK=true,saveBlocked=false,lastSaved=null,recoveredSave=false;
try {
  const raw=localStorage.getItem(KEY);
  if(raw){
    try { state=validate(JSON.parse(raw)); lastSaved=raw; }
    catch(error){
      try { state=validate(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY+'.backup'))); recoveredSave=true; }
      catch(backupError){ saveBlocked=true; storageOK=false; }
    }
  }
} catch(error){storageOK=false;saveBlocked=true;}
let route={view:saveBlocked?'recovery':state.heroChosen?'home':'characters'},pending=state.battle?.question||null,lastReward=null;
let previewHero=state.hero,heroFilter='All';const app=document.querySelector('#app');
function validate(s){if(!s||s.version!==1||!Number.isInteger(s.hero)||s.hero<0||s.hero>=HEROES.length||!Array.isArray(s.done)||!Array.isArray(s.read)||!['xp','gold','correct','answered'].every(k=>Number.isSafeInteger(s[k])&&s[k]>=0))throw Error('Invalid save');if(s.correct>s.answered)throw Error('Invalid question totals');for(const list of [s.done,s.read])if(list.some(x=>typeof x!=='string'||!/^\d+-\d+$/.test(x)||!validQuest(...x.split('-').map(Number))))throw Error('Invalid quest');if(typeof s.heroChosen!=='boolean')s.heroChosen=true;s.done=[...new Set(s.done)];s.read=[...new Set(s.read)];migrateGear(s);validateExam(s);validateAcademy(s);validateSkills(s);if(s.battle){const b=s.battle;if(!validQuest(b.r,b.c)||!['hp','enemy','shield','round'].every(k=>Number.isFinite(b[k])&&b[k]>=0)||b.hp>140||b.enemy>maxEnemy(b.c)||!Array.isArray(b.used)||b.used.some(x=>!Number.isInteger(x)||x<0||x>=realms.length)||!Array.isArray(b.log)||b.log.some(x=>typeof x!=='string'))throw Error('Invalid battle');if(b.maxHp===undefined)b.maxHp=100;if(!Number.isInteger(b.maxHp)||b.maxHp<100||b.maxHp>140||b.hp>b.maxHp)throw Error('Invalid health');if(b.resistance===undefined)b.resistance=0;if(!Number.isInteger(b.resistance)||b.resistance<0||b.resistance>5)throw Error('Invalid resistance');if(!Number.isInteger(b.round)||b.hp<=0||b.enemy<=0||b.shield>24)throw Error('Invalid battle');b.log=b.log.slice(-10);if(b.questionOrder!==undefined&&(!Array.isArray(b.questionOrder)||b.questionOrder.length>realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][4].length||b.questionOrder.length<1||new Set(b.questionOrder).size!==b.questionOrder.length||b.questionOrder.some(n=>!Number.isInteger(n)||n<0||n>=realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][4].length)||!Number.isInteger(b.questionCursor)||b.questionCursor<0||b.questionCursor>b.questionOrder.length))throw Error('Invalid question deck');if(b.question){const q=b.question;if(!Number.isInteger(q.index)||q.index<0||q.index>=realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][4].length||typeof q.answered!=='boolean'||(q.answered&&typeof q.right!=='boolean'))throw Error('Invalid question');}if(!b.loadout)b.loadout=gearStats(s);if(b.loadout.heal===undefined)b.loadout.heal=gearStats(s).heal;if(![0,25,40,60].includes(b.loadout.heal))throw Error('Invalid potion');if(!['attack','knowledge','guard'].every(k=>Number.isFinite(b.loadout[k]))||b.loadout.attack<10||b.loadout.attack>18||b.loadout.knowledge<20||b.loadout.knowledge>54||b.loadout.guard<0||b.loadout.guard>6)throw Error('Invalid battle gear');}return s;}
function save(){
  if(!saveBlocked){
    try {
      const next=JSON.stringify(state);
      if(next!==lastSaved){
        // Retain the previous valid state before replacing the primary save.
        if(lastSaved) localStorage.setItem(KEY+'.backup',lastSaved);
        localStorage.setItem(KEY,next);
        lastSaved=next;
      }
      storageOK=true;
    }catch(error){storageOK=false;}
  }
  document.querySelector('#saveStatus').textContent=storageOK?(recoveredSave?'✓ Recovered from backup':'✓ Saved on this device'):'Save unavailable · export a backup';
}
function recovery(){app.innerHTML=`<section class="lesson"><h1>Let’s protect your adventure.</h1><p>Your saved adventure could not be loaded. It has been left untouched.</p><p>Open your grimoire to import an exported save, or download the unreadable save before starting again.</p><button onclick="downloadDamagedSave()">Download original save</button><button onclick="startFresh()">Start a new adventure</button></section>`;}
function downloadDamagedSave(){try{downloadSave(localStorage.getItem(KEY)||'', 'certquest-recovery.json');}catch(error){toast('Browser storage is unavailable.');}}
function startFresh(){if(!window.confirm('Start over? Download your original save first if you want to keep it.'))return;state=fresh();lastSaved=null;saveBlocked=false;recoveredSave=false;go('characters');}
function downloadSave(data,name){const u=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([data],{type:'application/json'}));const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=u;a.download=name;a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(u),1000);}
const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));const id=(r,c)=>`${r}-${c}`;const level=()=>1+Math.floor(state.xp/100);function toast(t){const el=document.querySelector('#toast');el.textContent=t;el.style.display='block';setTimeout(()=>el.style.display='none',2800)}
function sprite(enemy=false){const h=HEROES[state.hero];const foe=realms[state.battle?.r||0].enemyArt||['forge-guardian','storm-drake','shadow-sovereign'][state.battle?.r||0];return `<div class="battle-portrait ${enemy?'foe-portrait':'hero-portrait'}"><img src="assets/${enemy?foe:h.id}.png?v=simple2" alt="${enemy?realms[state.battle.r].chapters[state.battle.c][2]:h.name}" width="400" height="500"></div>`;}
function go(view,r,c){if(saveBlocked)view='recovery';pending=view==='battle'?(state.battle?.question||null):null;route={view,r,c};render();window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function render(){save();if(route.view==='recovery')return recovery();if(route.view==='academy')return academy();if(route.view==='skills')return skillCatalog();if(route.view==='skill-lesson')return skillLesson(route.r,route.c);if(route.view==='characters')characters();if(route.view==='hero')heroSheet();if(route.view==='exam')examScreen();if(route.view==='home')home();if(route.view==='realm')realm(route.r);if(route.view==='lesson')lesson(route.r,route.c);if(route.view==='battle')battle();if(route.view==='reward')reward(route.r,route.c);}
function home(){app.innerHTML=`<section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">A little studying. A grand adventure.</div><h1>Knowledge is<br>your strongest spell.</h1><p>Five realms have fallen into shadow. Learn the craft, earn your magic, and bring the light back—one quest at a time.</p><button class="primary" onclick="continueQuest()">${state.battle?'Resume your battle':state.academy?.session&&!state.academy.session.submitted?'Resume your study session':'Continue your adventure'} →</button></div><button class="camp-hero" onclick="openHero()" aria-label="View your hero, ${HEROES[state.hero].name}"><img src="assets/${HEROES[state.hero].id}.png?v=simple2" alt="${HEROES[state.hero].name}" width="400" height="500"><span><small>YOUR ADVENTURER</small><strong>${HEROES[state.hero].name}</strong><em>View gear & inventory ↗</em></span></button></section><div class="camp-equipment"><div><span class="tag">Your loadout</span>${equipmentBadges()}</div><button onclick="openHero()">Your hero & inventory →</button></div><div class="status"><span>✦ Level <strong>${level()}</strong> ${HEROES[state.hero].name}</span><span class="grow">${state.xp} XP · ${state.done.length}/${questCount()} quests cleared</span><span>◈ <strong>${state.gold}</strong> gold</span></div><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Choose your path</div><h2>The five realms</h2></div><span class="muted">Explore in any order</span></div><div class="grid">${realms.map((r,i)=>{let n=state.done.filter(d=>d.startsWith(i+'-')).length;const study=STUDY_TOPICS.filter(t=>i===0?[1,2].includes(t.core):t.core===i+2),cleared=study.filter(t=>state.academy?.done.includes(t.id)).length;return `<article class="realm"><div class="icon">${r.icon}</div><div class="tag">${r.cert} · ${r.role}</div><h3>${r.name}</h3><p>${r.desc}</p><div class="bar"><span style="width:${cleared/study.length*100}%"></span></div><small class="muted">${cleared}/${study.length} study branches · ${realmUnlocked(i)?r.spell+' unlocked':'Unlock '+r.spell}</small><button onclick="openStudyCertification(${i})">${cleared===study.length?'Review certification':'Study certification'} →</button>${realmCourseLinks(i)}</article>`}).join('')}</div><p class="footer-note">OpenAI-generated fantasy art · No timers, no lost XP on defeat · Foundational study practice, not a complete certification course.</p>`;}
function continueQuest(){if(state.battle)return go('battle');if(state.academy?.session&&!state.academy.session.submitted)return academyTrial();const next=STUDY_TOPICS.find(t=>!state.academy?.done.includes(t.id)&&t.requires.every(k=>state.academy?.done.includes(k)));if(next)return academyLore(next.id);for(let r=0;r<realms.length;r++)for(let c=0;c<realms[r].chapters.length;c++)if(!state.done.includes(id(r,c)))return go('lesson',r,c);go('realm',0)}
function realm(r){let a=realms[r];app.innerHTML=`<button class="back" onclick="go('home')">← World map</button><div class="eyebrow">${a.cert} · ${a.role}</div><h1>${a.name}</h1><p class="muted">${a.desc} Clear the first quest to unlock ${a.spell} across every realm.</p><div class="quest-list">${a.chapters.map((q,c)=>{let done=state.done.includes(id(r,c)),open=c===0||state.done.includes(id(r,c-1));return `<div class="quest-row"><span class="num">${done?'✓':'0'+(c+1)}</span><div class="grow"><h3>${q[0]}</h3><p>${q[1]} · ${c===2?'Realm boss':'Encounter'}: ${q[2]}<br><span class="quest-reward-hint">Reward: ${ITEMS.find(i=>i.quest===id(r,c)).name}${done?' · collected':''}</span></p></div><button ${open?'':'disabled'} onclick="go('lesson',${r},${c})">${done?'Practice again':open?'Begin quest →':'Complete previous quest'}</button></div>`}).join('')}</div>${examConfig(r)?examGate(r):''}`;}
function lesson(r,c){let q=realms[r].chapters[c];app.innerHTML=`<section class="lesson"><button class="back" onclick="go('realm',${r})">← ${realms[r].name}</button><div class="eyebrow">Quest ${c+1} · Field notes</div><h1>${q[0]}</h1><p class="muted">${q[1]}</p>${realms[r].source?`<p><a class="study-link" href="${realms[r].source}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official ${realms[r].code} study guide ↗</a></p>`:''}<article class="paper"><h2>The lore you need</h2>${q[3].split('. ').map(s=>`<details><summary>${s}${s.endsWith('.')?'':'.'}</summary><p>${/encrypt/i.test(s)?'Encryption transforms readable data using a key. It protects confidentiality. Hashing checks integrity, and backups support recovery: these solve different problems. Losing the decryption key can make protected data unrecoverable.':/RAM|memory|storage/i.test(s)?'Distinguish working memory from persistent storage. Compare volatility, compatibility and the symptom before replacing hardware. The A+ field manual includes a memory-to-storage diagram and diagnostic scenarios.':'Connect this concept to a concrete symptom, identify what evidence would confirm it, and choose the least disruptive reasonable action. Open the workshop field manual for topic explanations and worked scenarios.'}</p><button onclick="studyBook()">Open field manual →</button></details>`).join('')}<strong>In battle: use a normal attack anytime, or answer a question for a powerful spell. Wrong answers include a hint and still advance the fight.</strong></article><button class="primary" onclick="begin(${r},${c})">Enter ${c===2?'the boss battle':'the encounter'} →</button><p class="muted">Your place in battle saves after every turn. Fleeing costs no earned progress.</p></section>`;if(!state.read.includes(id(r,c))){state.read.push(id(r,c));save();}}
function enemyType(r,c){return r===0?['physical','software','security'][c]:r===1?'network':r===2?'security':'software';}
function maxEnemy(c){return [90,120,160][c];}
function begin(r,c){if(state.battle&&(state.battle.r!==r||state.battle.c!==c)){toast('Finish or flee your current battle first.');return go('battle');}if(!state.battle)state.battle={r,c,hp:learningBonuses().maxHp,maxHp:learningBonuses().maxHp,resistance:learningBonuses().resistance[enemyType(r,c)],enemy:maxEnemy(c),shield:0,round:0,used:[],loadout:gearStats(),log:['The encounter begins. Your knowledge is your advantage.']};go('battle');}
function battle(){let b=state.battle;if(!b)return go('home');let q=realms[b.r].chapters[b.c];app.innerHTML=`<button class="back" onclick="go('home')">← Return to camp (battle saved)</button><div class="eyebrow">${realms[b.r].cert} · ${b.c===2?'Realm boss':'Encounter'} ${b.c+1}</div><h2>${q[2]}</h2><p style="color:${DAMAGE_TYPES[enemyType(b.r,b.c)].color}">${DAMAGE_TYPES[enemyType(b.r,b.c)].label} attacks · resistance ${b.resistance||0}</p><div class="arena"><div class="fighters"><div class="fighter"><span class="tag">${HEROES[state.hero].name}</span>${sprite()}<strong>${HEROES[state.hero].name.split(' ')[0]} · ${b.hp}/${b.maxHp||100} HP</strong><div class="bar"><span style="width:${b.hp/(b.maxHp||100)*100}%"></span></div>${b.shield?'<small>Shield: '+b.shield+'</small>':''}<div class="battle-loadout">${equipmentBadges()}</div></div><span class="vs">vs.</span><div class="fighter"><span class="tag">${b.c===2?'Boss of the realm':'Shadow creature'}</span>${sprite(true)}<strong>${b.enemy}/${maxEnemy(b.c)} HP</strong><div class="bar"><span style="width:${b.enemy/maxEnemy(b.c)*100}%"></span></div></div></div></div><div class="battle-bottom"><div><div class="actions"><button onclick="attack()" ${pending?'disabled':''}>⚔ Attack · ${combatStats().attack} damage</button><button class="primary" onclick="ask()" ${pending?'disabled':''}>✦ Knowledge spell · ${combatStats().knowledge}</button>${realms.map((r,i)=>realmUnlocked(i)?`<button onclick="ability(${i})" ${pending||b.used.includes(i)||(i===1&&(!combatStats().heal||b.hp===(b.maxHp||100)))?'disabled':''}>${i===1?'Drink potion · +'+combatStats().heal+' HP':r.spell}${b.used.includes(i)?' · used':''}</button>`:'').join('')}</div><p class="muted">Correct answers deal ${combatStats().knowledge} damage with your level and gear. Armor and shields block ${combatStats().guard} damage per enemy hit.</p><button onclick="flee()">Flee to camp</button></div><div class="log" aria-live="polite">${b.log.slice(-5).map(l=>`<p>${esc(l)}</p>`).join('')}</div></div><div id="question"></div>`;if(pending)drawQuestion();}
function turn(damage,message){let b=state.battle;b.enemy=Math.max(0,b.enemy-damage);b.log.push(message);b.round++;if(b.enemy<=0){const r=b.r,c=b.c;const first=!state.done.includes(id(r,c));if(first){state.done.push(id(r,c));state.xp+=100;state.gold+=50+(c===2?50:0);}const loot=first?grantLoot(r,c):{autoEquipped:false};lastReward={first,autoEquipped:loot.autoEquipped};state.battle=null;pending=null;save();return go('reward',r,c);}let hit=Math.max(1,7+b.c*2-combatStats().guard-(b.resistance||0));let blocked=Math.min(b.shield,hit);b.shield-=blocked;hit-=blocked;b.hp=Math.max(0,b.hp-hit);b.log.push(`${realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][2]} strikes for ${hit}${blocked?' ('+blocked+' blocked)':''}.`);b.log=b.log.slice(-10);if(b.hp===0){state.battle=null;pending=null;save();app.innerHTML=`<div class="reward"><div class="big">☾</div><h1>A moment to regroup.</h1><p>You return safely to camp. Your XP, spells, and completed quests are kept.</p><button class="primary" onclick="go('lesson',${b.r},${b.c})">Review the lore & retry</button><button onclick="go('home')">Return to camp</button></div>`;return;}save();battle();studyAnimation(damage>combatStats().attack?'spell':'attack');}
function attack(){if(pending||!state.battle)return;const d=combatStats().attack;turn(d,`Your attack hits for ${d} damage.`);}
function ask(){if(pending||!state.battle)return;let b=state.battle,q=realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][4];b.questionOrder??=studyShuffle(q.map((_,i)=>i));b.questionCursor??=0;if(b.questionCursor>=b.questionOrder.length){b.questionOrder=studyShuffle(q.map((_,i)=>i));b.questionCursor=0;}pending={index:b.questionOrder[b.questionCursor++],answered:false};b.question=pending;save();battle();}
function drawQuestion(){let b=state.battle,q=realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][4][pending.index];document.querySelector('#question').innerHTML=`<section class="quiz"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#58704e">Channel your knowledge</div><h3>${q[0]}</h3><div class="answers">${q[1].map((a,i)=>`<button onclick="answer(${i})" ${pending.answered?'disabled':''}>${String.fromCharCode(65+i)}. ${a}</button>`).join('')}</div>${pending.answered?`<div class="feedback" role="status"><strong>${pending.right?'Correct! Your spell is empowered.':'A miscast—but you learn from it.'}</strong><br>${q[3]}<br><button style="margin-top:12px" class="primary" onclick="resolveAnswer()">Cast for ${pending.right?combatStats().knowledge:5} damage →</button></div>`:''}</section>`;}
function answer(i){if(!pending||pending.answered)return;let b=state.battle,q=realms[b.r].chapters[b.c][4][pending.index];pending.answered=true;pending.right=i===q[2];save();drawQuestion();}
function resolveAnswer(){if(!pending?.answered)return;let right=pending.right;delete state.battle.question;state.answered++;if(right)state.correct++;let d=right?combatStats().knowledge:5;pending=null;turn(d,right?`Knowledge spell deals ${d} damage!`:'Your spell flickers for 5 damage. Try the next question.');}
function ability(i){let b=state.battle;if(!Number.isInteger(i)||!realms[i]||!b||pending||b.used.includes(i)||!realmUnlocked(i))return;if(i===1){if(!combatStats().heal||b.hp===(b.maxHp||100))return;const healed=Math.min(combatStats().heal,(b.maxHp||100)-b.hp);b.hp+=healed;b.used.push(1);b.log.push(`You drink your potion and recover ${healed} HP. It refills next battle.`);b.log=b.log.slice(-10);save();battle();studyAnimation('heal');return;}b.used.push(i);if(i===0){b.hp=Math.min(b.maxHp||100,b.hp+26);turn(0,'Mending Light restores up to 26 health.');}if(i===2)turn(26,'Cipher Strike deals 26 damage!');if(i===3){const damage=combatStats().knowledge+8;turn(damage,`Elastic Burst scales up for ${damage} damage!`);}if(i===4){b.shield=24;turn(0,'Availability Ward absorbs up to 24 incoming damage.');}}
function flee(){state.battle=null;pending=null;save();go('home');toast('Returned safely. Earned progress kept.');}
function reward(r,c){app.innerHTML=`<div class="reward"><div class="big">✧</div><div class="eyebrow">Quest complete</div><h1>${c===2?'The realm is restored.':'A little wiser. A little stronger.'}</h1><p>${realms[r].chapters[c][2]} has fallen. ${lastReward?.first?'You earned 100 XP and '+(c===2?100:50)+' gold.':'Practice complete. Your earned gear and progress stay with you.'}</p>${lootReward(r,c)}${examConfig(r)&&c===realms[r].chapters.length-1?examGate(r):''}${c===0&&lastReward?.first?`<article class="paper"><h2>${realms[r].spell} unlocked</h2><p>${realms[r].effect} Available in every realm.</p></article>`:''}<button class="primary" onclick="go('${c<2?'lesson':'home'}',${r},${c+1})">${c<2?'Next quest →':'Return to the world map'}</button><p class="muted">Progress saved automatically.</p></div>`;}
document.querySelector('#journalBtn').onclick=()=>{document.querySelector('#journalContent').innerHTML=`<p>Level ${level()} · ${state.xp} XP · ${state.gold} gold<br>${state.done.length}/${questCount()} quests · ${state.correct}/${state.answered} battle questions correct</p><div class="journal-hero"><img src="assets/${HEROES[state.hero].id}.png?v=simple2" alt="${HEROES[state.hero].name}"><div><h3>${HEROES[state.hero].name}</h3><p class="muted">${HEROES[state.hero].role}</p><button onclick="openCharacters()">Change appearance ↗</button></div></div><p class="muted">Your hero keeps the same gear and progress through every realm.</p><button onclick="openHero()">Equipment & inventory →</button><h3>Your magic</h3>${realms.map((r,i)=>`<div class="spell"><strong>${realmUnlocked(i)?'✦':'◇'} ${r.spell}</strong><br><span class="muted">${realmUnlocked(i)?r.effect:'Clear the first '+r.cert+' quest to unlock.'}</span></div>`).join('')}`;document.querySelector('#journal').showModal();};
function chooseHero(i){if(!Number.isInteger(i)||!HEROES[i])return;state.hero=i;state.heroChosen=true;save();go('home');toast(HEROES[i].name+' joins your adventure.');}
function openCharacters(){document.querySelector('#journal').close();previewHero=state.hero;heroFilter='All';go('characters');}
function previewCharacter(i){if(!HEROES[i])return;previewHero=i;characters();}
function filterHeroes(filter){if(!['All','Artificer','Wayfinder','Sentinel'].includes(filter))return;heroFilter=filter;if(filter!=='All'&&HEROES[previewHero].role!==filter)previewHero=HEROES.findIndex(h=>h.role===filter);characters();}
function characters(){const h=HEROES[previewHero];app.innerHTML=`<section class="character-page"><div class="character-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Your adventure begins with you</div><h1>Choose your adventurer.</h1><p class="muted">Six heroes. Three callings. A whole world to discover.</p></div>${state.heroChosen?'<button class="back" onclick="go(\'home\')">← Return to camp</button>':''}</div><div class="selection-layout"><div class="roster"><div class="roster-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by calling">${['All','Artificer','Wayfinder','Sentinel'].map(f=>`<button aria-pressed="${heroFilter===f}" onclick="filterHeroes('${f}')">${f==='All'?'All heroes':f+'s'}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="character-grid">${HEROES.map((hero,i)=>heroFilter!=='All'&&hero.role!==heroFilter?'':`<button class="character-card ${previewHero===i?'selected':''}" aria-pressed="${previewHero===i}" aria-label="Preview ${hero.name}, ${hero.role}" onclick="previewCharacter(${i})" style="--accent:${hero.color}"><div class="character-image"><img src="assets/${hero.id}.png?v=simple2" alt="" width="400" height="500" ${i>2?'loading="lazy"':''}></div><div class="character-caption"><small>${hero.role} · ${hero.path}</small><strong>${hero.name}</strong><span>${state.heroChosen&&state.hero===i?'Your current hero':previewHero===i?'Selected for preview':'View character'} ${previewHero===i?'✦':'↗'}</span></div></button>`).join('')}</div><p class="selection-note">All six heroes are available from the start. Choose the hero you will grow throughout the adventure. Quest rewards and equipment follow you through every realm.</p></div><aside class="hero-detail" style="--accent:${h.color}" aria-label="Character preview"><div class="detail-art"><img src="assets/${h.id}.png?v=simple2" alt="Full illustration of ${h.name}" width="400" height="500"></div><div class="detail-copy"><span class="tag">${h.role} · ${h.path} affinity</span><h2>${h.name}</h2><p class="hero-quote">“${h.line}”</p><p>${h.bio}</p><div class="hero-gear">${h.gear}</div><button class="primary" onclick="chooseHero(${previewHero})">${state.heroChosen&&state.hero===previewHero?'Continue as '+h.name.split(' ')[0]:'Choose '+h.name.split(' ')[0]+' →'}</button><small>Your hero, equipment, and progress save automatically. Changing appearance keeps everything you have earned.</small></div></aside></div></section>`;}
document.querySelector('#charactersBtn').onclick=openCharacters;document.querySelector('#heroBtn').onclick=openHero;
document.querySelector('#export').onclick=()=>{if(saveBlocked)return downloadDamagedSave();downloadSave(JSON.stringify(state,null,2),'certquest-save.json');toast('Save exported.');};
document.querySelector('#import').onchange=async e=>{try{let f=e.target.files[0];if(!f)return;if(f.size>2000000)throw Error();let next=validate(JSON.parse(await f.text()));if((state.done.length||Object.keys(state.skills||{}).length)&&!window.confirm('Replace this adventure with the imported save? Export your current adventure first if you want to keep both.'))return;state=next;saveBlocked=false;recoveredSave=false;save();document.querySelector('#journal').close();go(state.heroChosen?'home':'characters');toast('Adventure restored.');}catch(err){toast('That file is not a valid CertQuest save.');}e.target.value='';};
render();


function realmCourseLinks(realm){const courses=Object.entries(CERTIFICATIONS).filter(([,c])=>c.parent&&c.realm===realm);return courses.length?`<details class="realm-courses"><summary>More certifications · ${courses.length}</summary>${courses.map(([core,c])=>`<button class="advanced-path" onclick="showQuestMap(${core})">${core<=8?'Advanced path':core==14?'Linux path':'Study path'} · ${esc(c.name)} →</button>`).join('')}</details>`:'';}
